{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q6784821","formula":"C₁₀H₁₆O₂","hill":"C10H16O2","elements":["H","C","O"],"composition":{"C":10.0,"H":16.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"(R)-Massoia lactone"},"descriptions":{"en":"Massoia lactone is an alkyl lactone derived from the bark of the Massoia tree (Cryptocaria massoia) which is found in Papua, Indonesia though the compound can also be found as a component of cane sugar molasses, cured tobacco, and the essential oil of Sweet Osmanthus (Osmanthus fragrans). Chemically, massoia lactone can be obtained as a minor product in transfer hydrogenation of 6-amyl-α-pyrone. Known in the late 18th and early 19th centuries as massoy bark, massoia essential oil was once widely used as a natural coconut flavouring."},"fame":6,"pubchemCid":642793,"mass":168.23,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCC[C@@H]1CC=CC(=O)O1","inchikey":"NEDIAPMWNCQWNW-SECBINFHSA-N","iupac":"(2R)-2-pentyl-2,3-dihydropyran-6-one","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"642793","atoms":28,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.078,"y":0.632,"z":-0.2,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.625,"y":2.29,"z":-0.155,"el":"O"},{"x":0.655,"y":-1.026,"z":-0.227,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.744,"y":-0.692,"z":0.271,"el":"C"},{"x":1.688,"y":-0.029,"z":0.297,"el":"C"},{"x":3.098,"y":-0.387,"z":-0.177,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.767,"y":-1.707,"z":-0.22,"el":"C"},{"x":4.127,"y":0.629,"z":0.319,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.135,"y":-1.206,"z":0.098,"el":"C"},{"x":5.524,"y":0.294,"z":-0.179,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.346,"y":1.101,"z":-0.046,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.396,"y":0.099,"z":0.218,"el":"C"},{"x":0.673,"y":-1.003,"z":-1.323,"el":"H"},{"x":0.928,"y":-2.04,"z":0.087,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.738,"y":-0.658,"z":1.369,"el":"H"},{"x":1.442,"y":0.984,"z":-0.043,"el":"H"},{"x":1.666,"y":-0.015,"z":1.394,"el":"H"},{"x":3.365,"y":-1.388,"z":0.183,"el":"H"},{"x":3.117,"y":-0.